- Query the USGS Earthquake API at
  https://earthquake.usgs.gov/fdsnws/event/1/query
- Request all earthquakes from the past 30 days with magnitude >= 2.0
- Bounding box: latitude 32-49, longitude -125 to -114 (western US)
- Request format: GeoJSON
- No authentication required

PROCESSING:
- Use whatever magnitude scale the USGS API returns natively (ml or mw)
- Drop any rows with null or missing magnitude or depth values
- Use raw latitude/longitude coordinates directly — no reprojection
- Map raw depth values in km directly to the plasma colormap,
  letting matplotlib scale the range automatically from the
  dataset min/max depth
- Size points using an exponential scale where each unit increase in
  magnitude doubles the marker area — use a base size of 80 and scale
  relative to the dataset's actual magnitude range,
  e.g. size = 80 * (2 ** (magnitude - mag_min))

OUTPUT:
